    {
      "block_id": "2605.24807_p7_b12",
      "text": "We train SAM and CLIP end-to-end using supervision only on SAM\u2019s out-\nput masks. Since thresholding used for binary similarity mask prompt is non-\ndifferentiable, gradients reach CLIP only through the injected feature pathway.\nWe optimize a standard segmentation loss L = LBCE+LDice+LIoU. We fine-tune\nonly CLIP\u2019s vision encoder\u2019s attention blocks while freezing the MLP blocks and\nthe text encoder; for SAM, we fine-tune the prompt encoder, mask decoder, and\nthe inserted adapters.\n",
      "bbox": [
